  "result": "All 6 tests pass (both test files). Summary of changes, all in `catalog/service.py`:\n\n- **`find(substring)`**: case-insensitive substring match on title using `casefold`, returns copies of records in creation order.\n- **`export()`**: returns `json.dumps` of `list()`, so the dump is a JSON array in creation order.\n- **`import_(dump)`**: parses the dump, validates that it is an array of `{id, title, author}` string records, and inserts them keeping their ids. It works on an empty or populated catalog. Two judgment calls worth knowing:\n  - A duplicate id, either within the dump or against an existing record, raises `ValueError` and imports nothing, rather than silently overwriting.\n  - Since this catalog uses sequential integer ids, the counter is advanced past the largest numeric imported id so later `create()` calls cannot collide with imported records. Non-numeric ids from other implementations are accepted as-is.\n\nNo files under `tests/` were touched.",
